Portable shell and tool configuration, promoted deliberately from the canonical
source configs. This is a public repository: local credentials, histories,
machine state and entire home directories are not synchronization inputs.

`just sync` previews differences for the individual files in `sync-files.txt`.
It is always a dry run, performs no deletions and does not copy changes. Review
the source contents and Git diff before applying selected changes. There is no
FOLDERS override or whole-directory copy recipe.

Zsh and Neovim are separate repositories under `.config/`. Review and commit
their source changes first, then select those commits here. A dirty submodule
checkout is a review preview; the parent gitlink cannot record its uncommitted
files. Publication also requires making the referenced source commits available.

See [docs/sync-policy.md](docs/sync-policy.md) for the public file boundary,
intentional platform differences and the separate agent configuration review.
The appearance assets and installation requirements are described in
[docs/terminal-appearance.md](docs/terminal-appearance.md).

The current Zsh parity changes, runtime policy, and quick regression commands are
documented in [docs/zsh-parity.md](docs/zsh-parity.md).


